Hello. The use lowered lower limb exoskeletons has received praise for the positive impact they have had on gait for individuals with cerebral palsy. However, current data is scanty as this research on this new technology is still in its early stages. You can find some of the data linked bellow;

1) Lerner ZF, Damiano DL, Park HS, Gravunder AJ, Bulea TC. (2017). A robotic exoskeleton for treatment of crouch gait in children with cerebral palsy: design and initial application.(external link) IEEE Trans Neural Syst Rehabil Eng. Jun;25(6):650-659. doi:10.1109/TNSRE.2016.2595501.

2)Lerner ZF, Damiano DL, Bulea TC. (2017). A lower-extremity exoskeleton improves knee extension in children with crouch gait from cerebral palsy.(external link) Sci Transl Med. Aug 23;9(404):eaam9145. doi:10.1126/scitranslmed.aam9145.
